Detection of Open-Cast Mining Visualization
Problem Statement

Open-cast mining activities cause significant changes to land surfaces, vegetation cover, and the surrounding environment. Traditional methods of monitoring mining areas are time-consuming, expensive, and often rely on manual inspections. There is a need for an automated system that can accurately detect and visualize open-cast mining regions from satellite or aerial imagery. Such a system would help authorities, environmental agencies, and researchers monitor mining activities, track land-use changes, and assess environmental impacts efficiently.

Project Objectives
To collect and preprocess satellite images for mining area analysis.
To identify and extract relevant features associated with open-cast mining regions.
To develop a detection model using image processing and machine learning/deep learning techniques.
To classify mining and non-mining areas accurately.
To visualize detected open-cast mining regions on satellite images.
To monitor land-cover changes caused by mining activities over time.
To improve detection accuracy and reduce manual effort in mining area monitoring.
To generate useful outputs for environmental assessment and decision-making.
Module List
Module 1: Data Collection
Gather satellite or aerial images from public datasets.
Organize image datasets for training and testing.
Module 2: Image Preprocessing
Resize images.
Remove noise and enhance image quality.
Normalize image data for analysis.
Module 3: Feature Extraction
Extract texture, color, and shape features.
Identify characteristics of open-cast mining areas.
Module 4: Mining Area Detection
Apply machine learning or deep learning algorithms.
Detect mining regions from satellite images.
Module 5: Classification
Classify images into mining and non-mining categories.
Evaluate classification performance.
Module 6: Visualization
Highlight detected mining regions.
Display results using bounding boxes, masks, or heat maps.
Module 7: Change Detection Analysis
Compare historical and current images.
Identify expansion or reduction of mining areas.
Module 8: Result Generation and Reporting
Generate detection reports.
Display accuracy metrics and visual outputs.
Store and export analysis results.
Expected Outcome

The proposed system will automatically detect and visualize open-cast mining areas from satellite imagery, providing accurate monitoring of mining activities and supporting environmental management through efficient geospatial analysis.
